WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.580
A piece of barium in cold water fizzes hard,
bubbles of hydrogen streaming off it.

2
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:11.460
Magnesium, from the same group,
sits in cold water and barely reacts.

3
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.240
A few slow bubbles, nothing more.

4
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:19.140
Yet heat magnesium in steam, and it
burns with a bright white light.

5
00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.580
Same group, same kind of metal.

6
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:26.360
So why does barium fizz in cold
water when magnesium barely reacts?

7
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.020
In this mission, you'll watch the
Group 2 metals react with water,

8
00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.860
and write the equation for each reaction.

9
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.960
Then you'll trace the
trends down the group,

10
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:38.040
and use real data to explain the pattern.

11
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:43.810
Your mission: explain why barium fizzes in
cold water while magnesium hardly reacts.